{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sdp_cannot_force_top_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sdp_cannot_force_top_degree","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L171-L206","doc":"**THE CRUX (limitative).**  There exist two graded assignments — the\nsingle-degree Springer object `G_λ = singleCoeffs` and the full fake-degree\ncoinvariant object `H_λ = fakeCoeffs` — such that:\n\n  • they carry the SAME ungraded Wedderburn dimension `dim V_λ` at every\n    block (`same`), i.e. they are INDISTINGUISHABLE to any functional of the\n    ungraded block data — which is *exactly* what the confinement SDP\n    (`ρ_λ(T(c)) ⪰ 0`), the canonical `T_w` selection, and the Markov trace\n    `tr_M = Σ_λ w_λ χ_λ` are (they factor through `⊕_λ End(V_λ)`);\n\n  • yet their signed (DT/Behrend) Euler characteristics DIFFER on every\n    non-trivial block (`differ`), with only the single-degree object equal to\n    `Δ_λ` (`single_is_delta`).\n\nConsequently the ungraded datum does NOT pin the graded Euler characteristic,\nso NO functional of it — in particular the confinement SDP / canonical `T_w`\n— can FORCE the top-degree (single-degree) concentration.  The top-cohomology\nprojection `H^{top}(𝓑_λ) = V_λ` is a genuinely INDEPENDENT input.  This is the\nprecise NEGATIVE answer to bean `qou-nmpr`: the confinement SDP / canonical\n`T_w`, as constructed, does not reach top degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_gradedEuler_ne_deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fake_gradedEuler_ne_deltaLambda","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L157-L167","doc":"**The full fake-degree object does NOT realize `Δ_λ`** on any non-trivial\nblock: `f_λ(-1) ≠ Δ_λ` whenever `dim V_λ > 1`.  So the single-degree\nconcentration (top-cohomology selection) is LOAD-BEARING — dropping it and\nkeeping the full coinvariant grading breaks the identity at every block that\nis not already a single degree.  (Extends PR #4559's `λ=(2,1)`, `n=3`,\n`f(-1)=0≠-2` observation to the entire `n=5` anchor.  The two dim-1 blocks\n`(5)`, `(1⁵)` are trivially single-degree monomials, so they agree — hence the\n`dim ≠ 1` hypothesis.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.single_gradedEuler_eq_deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.single_gradedEuler_eq_deltaLambda","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L151-L155","doc":"**The single-degree object realizes `Δ_λ`.**  Its Euler characteristic is\n`(-1)^{n(λ)}·dim V_λ = Δ_λ` (the collapse of PR #4553's `dtEuler`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.same_ungraded_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.same_ungraded_dim","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L144-L147","doc":"The two objects carry the same ungraded dimension, block by block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fakeTotalDim_eq_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fakeTotalDim_eq_dim","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L136-L142","doc":"The full fake-degree object ALSO totals to `dim V_λ` — this is `f_λ(1) =\ndim V_λ` (the number of standard Young tableaux).  Hence the ungraded datum\n`dim V_λ` — everything the confinement SDP / `T_w` / `tr_M` read — is SHARED\nbetween `G_λ` and `H_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.singleTotalDim_eq_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.singleTotalDim_eq_dim","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L131-L134","doc":"The single-degree object totals to `dim V_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fakeCoeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fakeCoeffs","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L114-L127","doc":"**The full fake-degree object `H_λ`.**  Graded dimensions `= coefficients of\nthe fake-degree polynomial `f_λ(q) = q^{n(λ)}·[5]_q! / ∏_{cell} [h]_q` (the\ngraded dimension of the `λ`-isotypic component of the `S_5`-coinvariant\nalgebra = graded `H^*(𝓑_λ)`).  Position `i` is the coefficient of `q^i`.\nHard-coded table (n=5) whose shape matches that polynomial; separately\nverified `f_λ(1) = dim V_λ` by `fakeTotalDim_eq_dim`, below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.singleCoeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.singleCoeffs","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L107-L112","doc":"**The single-degree Springer object `G_λ`.**  `dim V_λ` concentrated in the\nONE degree `n(λ)` (a-function `= dim_ℂ 𝓑_λ`), zero elsewhere: the\ncoefficient list is `n(λ)` zeros followed by `dim V_λ`.  This is the graded\nobject whose Euler characteristic is `Δ_λ` (PR #4553, `DeltaLambdaDTIndex`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.gradedEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.gradedEuler","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.gradedEulerAux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.gradedEulerAux","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaTopDegreeConcentration.lean#L99-L101","signatureChunk":0}]}